-- A regression guard for CK-37 (checker-v2.md §9.5; plans/checker-rewrite.md
-- §5.5): `x == [ x ]` makes `x`'s type contain itself. The resolver walk that
-- meets the cycle reports it ONCE, at the `==`, and poisons the cycle's root,
-- so the `<` on the same receiver adds nothing. 7427828 does exactly this
-- (round 4 probe `cyc1`); R6a keeps it green.
f x =
    x == [ x ] && x < [ x ]
